{
  "about": "Zotero boxes (text_box.zotero), on a real library's numbers: gamma/text_box.py and frontend/src/markup/textBox.js read these cases, and the Zotero sync's tests read `items`. `items` are three text annotations as Zotero's Web API returned them (the fields Gamma reads), each on its PDF page as shown (`page`, points, rotation 0, the view box from the origin), with the content and box a new block takes from it, the item's rect back from that box, and for an item already linked on the test server the block's box as it is stored there with the key added (`linked`). `layout` is gamma/text_box.py _layout on the same text as a Zotero box and as a Gamma box: each text row's text, x and baseline in points from the box's top-left, and the natural size. `frame` is zotero_frame of a box on a surface. `refit` is refitBox after the box rendered at `shown` on a surface `surface_width` wide; `merge` is merge_text_box / mergeTextBox. Widths are Helvetica's (the server's metrics); `segoe_width` is the line's width in Segoe UI, the face Zotero's reader and a Zotero box draw on Windows.",
  "items": [
